  Structure CONFIRMED (not assumed):
   - 19th-c biennial: oracle even-yr row -> production-YYYY-YY span dir (+ "-code" sibling =
     same session's code-amendment volume, SAME chapter numbering -> set-unioned, never summed).
   - transition 1901->production-1900-01, 1911->production-1910-11.
   - budget "-NNchapters" sub-volumes: the even-yr budget chapters are bound into the FOLLOWING
     odd-yr volume; suffix NN = budget calendar year (1953_Vol1_52Chapters.pdf = the 1952 chapters).
     Confirmed by source-PDF names under chief-clerk-archive/.

  SURPRISE A (1909 collision): 1909's data physically lives in production-1907-09 (certified
     confident max=729 == oracle 1909). BUT the existing greedy glob `production-1907*` already
     consumes production-1907-09 for oracle 1907 (capping it at 539). Note production-1906-07 is the
     truer 1907 volume (certified max=539). Aliasing 1909 to production-1907-09 = double-count.
     -> 1909 left UNMAPPED by design (data present, dir owned by 1907; remapping 1907 is out of scope).

  SURPRISE B (budget collision): the greedy odd-year glob `production-1953*` etc. ALSO sweeps the
     "-NNchapters" budget sub-volume into the adjacent odd-year regular session. Verified harmless:
     excluding the budget dir costs the odd years <=1 chapter total (only 1953 -1; all others 0 --
     budget chapters 1..N are already covered by the odd year's vol1). -> added BUDGET_OWNED_DIRS
     exclusion so the budget sub-volume is handed solely to the budget year's alias (no double-count).

  SURPRISE C (broken merge for 1901/1909/1911): parsed_acts_merged.json holds only the tiny extra-
     session fragment, but parsed_acts_certified.json holds the full session. Certified-confident
     ceiling (capped at N): 1901=252/275, 1909=544/729, 1911=394/753. This is a DATA/merge artifact,
     NOT a mapping artifact; the merge step must be re-run (out of scope for this measurement task).

